    97	closed subspaces, and an open set with compact closure around any compact set.
    98	That shrinking clause is exactly what a nested construction needs, and
    99	[[thm-baire-category-locally-compact-hausdorff]] runs one: every locally compact
   100	Hausdorff space is a Baire space ([[def-baire-space]]), assuming dependent
   101	choice. The construction shrinks at stage $n$ into the $n$-th dense open set, so
   102	the relation governing it changes with the stage;
   103	[[lem-dependent-choice-along-a-sequence-of-relations]] is the bridge from the
   104	single-relation form of dependent choice to that situation, and it is needed
   105	because a family of relations is not a relation.
